}

According to the [definition of LCA on Wikipedia](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lowestcommonancestor): "The lowest common ancestor of two nodes p and q in a tree T is the lowest node that has both p and q as descendants (where we allow a node to be a descendant of itself). "

